# Articles — no correction archaeology

When editing **reader-facing articles** (parent-folder essays under `paradigm-threat-files/`, not `investigations/` dossiers):

- State the **correct fact once**. Do **not** narrate how a draft was wrong.
- **Forbidden in article bodies:** “— not X”, “SRT-corrected”, “prior file error”, “we used to say”, “confirm on episode”, “embedded SRT shows”, “Office Ladies confirms”, session/audit chatter about your own fix.
- Put hygiene, SRT checks, and episode corrections in the **companion investigation** (changelog / Investigator notes) or keep them in chat.
- Follow `paradigm-threat-files/docs/instructions/ARTICLES.md` → **No drafting-process meta**.

Shipping assistant mistakes and corrections into the published essay is forbidden.
